From 6e373754dc90b42845a867adddf02dec7dbf94c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 07:10:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix launcher icon rendering completely black

Root cause: the previous fix scaled the (already very dark, mean
brightness ~25/255) artwork down to 72% and pasted it onto an extra
OPAQUE black canvas with no alpha channel. That stacked two layers
of blackness on top of an image that's already ~66% near-pure-black
by design, and at real launcher icon sizes (48-108px) the remaining
red glow/silhouette detail became imperceptible -- it read as a
solid black square.

Fix (regenerated the 10 foreground/round PNGs only -- artwork pixels
themselves are byte-for-byte from the same frozen source, nothing
redesigned):
- Foreground and round mipmaps are now true RGBA with real alpha
  transparency in the padding ring, instead of a second opaque black
  layer, so the background color shows through once instead of
  compounding with the source's own dark background.
- Reduced padding from 72% to 92% scale. The artwork's actual visible
  content already extends to ~96% of the frame (measured), so the
  previous heavy padding was throwing away most of the little
  breathing room the source has and made the content-to-black ratio
  far worse than necessary.
- Verified by compositing foreground over @color/ic_launcher_background
  exactly as Android would, then rendering that at realistic on-screen
  sizes (48/64px) -- the group of suspects, question mark, and
  magnifying glass are all clearly visible, not black.
- Re-checked the circular-mask worst case: the detective, question
  mark, and magnifying glass (dead center) are fully protected: only
  the outermost corner pixels of the artwork's own rounded-square
  border are touched, not any of the suspects.

Unchanged: ic_launcher.xml / ic_launcher_round.xml (structure was
already correct), AndroidManifest.xml (android:icon/roundIcon
already pointed at @mipmap/ic_launcher[_round]), colors.xml, the
plain full-bleed ic_launcher.png legacy assets, and all Java sources
(verified: only the 10 PNGs appear in this commit; MainActivity and
game logic untouched, and the project still compiles cleanly against
the same Android API stub set used throughout this project).
